Dimension-aware ranking of ER-expanded tables

Applies on top of hybrid-search-er-expansion.patch. Touches er_filter.py only.

The relationship filter previously admitted its expansion slots in fused order.
That is self-defeating: the fused score is exactly what failed to surface these
tables in the first place. Each connected candidate is now scored on four
signals normalised to [0,1], of which text rank is only one:

    score = 1.0 * rank          position within the pool, 1.0 at the top
          + 0.5 * dimension     dimension tables are first-class related tables
          + 0.3 * corroboration how many of the head's tables it joins
          + 0.2 * confidence    the graph's own edge-quality estimate

The three boosts sum to the rank weight on purpose: everything going right for
a candidate can at most fully compensate for sitting at the bottom of the pool,
never more. A dimension ranked last can reach, but not pass, an unboosted table
ranked first.

Dimensions are weighted because a fact table joins its dimensions — that is the
shape of the schema, and the dimensions carry the codes and descriptions a
question filters on. The cost is asymmetric too: a missing dimension breaks the
join, an unused one is ignored.

Includes a dimension detector that matches a whole "dim" segment anywhere in the
name, so snapshot variants (..._dim_actv) are classified as dimensions. The
existing helper tests endswith("dim") and misses them.

Knobs (env, read at import): ER_W_RANK, ER_W_DIM, ER_W_ANCHORS, ER_W_CONF,
ER_CORROBORATION_SPAN.

Table and column names in comments are placeholders.
